        body: "Each ad sells a concept (a contest, a story, a discovery), and the tune-up rides along, the way chess computers rode along with the Karpov challenge. Every twist must be real; invented drama would break the honesty Sugarman builds everything on. Watch price too: an $89 tune-up and a $29 tune-up don't just differ in margin; they say different things about the company."
