          model: "1) PMT: mid price; unusual for a non-rider (they can't picture it); a short video of the lot builds some environment. Verdict: medium-long, 100–150-word ad text, a landing page that answers 8–10 questions.\n2) Roof replacement: high price; familiar product but rare purchase; photos of past jobs help but trust is the issue. Verdict: long page (600+ words: process, materials, warranty, financing, reviews), ad text 100–200 words.\n3) $79 tune-up: low price, familiar; but if competitors charge $150, the price may need a sentence of credibility (“why so low: we do these in spring to keep crews busy”). Verdict: short, 30–60 words, plus one credibility line."
